/**
\page building_the_documentation Building the documentation

The documentation is built as part of the CMake build system.

\section doc_targets Targets

- \c docs -- runs Doxygen and produces the full HTML documentation in
  \c <buildDir>/doc/html.  Open \c doc/html/index.html in a browser.
  The rendered technical memos (\c PDF) are copied into the output
  tree under \c doc/html/tex and are reachable from the documentation
  home page and the \ref technical_memos "memo list."
- \c memos -- (re)builds the LaTeX technical memos in
  \c doc/docs/tex via \c latexmk.  Built automatically as a
  prerequisite of \c docs when \c latexmk is available.

\section doc_config Configuration options

| CMake option          | Default | Meaning                                        |
|-----------------------|---------|------------------------------------------------|
| SCUFF_BUILD_DOCS      | ON if Doxygen found | Enable the documentation targets   |
| SCUFF_BUILD_MEMOS     | ON if latexmk found | Rebuild the LaTeX memos from source|

\section doc_requirements Requirements

- Doxygen (1.9 or newer recommended) for the HTML documentation.
- \c pdflatex and \c latexmk with the standard TeX Live package set
  for rebuilding the memos from source.  Without them the committed
  PDFs are simply copied into the HTML output.
- The formulas on the documentation pages are rendered client-side by
  MathJax loaded from a public CDN, so the HTML documentation requires
  network access for formula display.

\section doc_source_source Documentation sources

- \c doc/docs -- the markdown documentation tree (tutorials, reference
  pages, application manuals).  The files were originally written for
  the mkdocs-based documentation site; a small input filter
  (\c doc/doxygen/md-filter.py) translates the few mkdocs-specific
  constructs (wikilinks, include directives) when Doxygen processes
  them.
- \c doc/docs/tex -- LaTeX sources of the technical memos.
- \c doc/dox -- the Doxygen-specific glue pages (this page, the API
  overview, the memo list).
- Library headers -- the API reference is extracted directly from the
  source code.

*/

